## Pitfall
The frequency resolution `fs/bs` must be finer than the half-power bandwidth of the modes, $2\xi f_n$. For the first mode, $2 \times 0.02 \times 2.28 \approx$ 0.09 Hz: with 4 s blocks (`bs = 1024`, resolution 0.25 Hz), the resonance peaks are smeared by the window, and the identification returns split modes and overestimated damping ratios. Lightly damped, low-frequency structures require long blocks, hence long records.
